39,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
40,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found some really interesting things! It turns out that transport costs change a lot depending on how far we go. Also, some people didn't come to the camps at all in the past! That's so sad!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Shizue,,It is indeed heartbreaking to see that some members didn't join us. I found that the seniors believe the only time different year-groups truly mingle is during the evenings when everyone stays together in one place.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The data reveals a significant administrative risk. Publicly run centers require a tedious lottery process and rigid paperwork that cannot easily be adjusted. Furthermore, self-catering is a major drain on time and labor.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that if we use our own hall, we'd have to train super early or super late because other clubs are there! That sounds like a total nightmare for our sleep!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"I found that public beds are quite affordable at 1,100 yen per night. However, whole-building lets are risky; since deposits are non-refundable, any last-minute cancellations would increase the cost for everyone else.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, that's a really scary point! If someone cancels and the cost goes up for everyone, that's not fair at all. I wonder if we've ever had to deal with that before? It makes me worried about the flat fee!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is a worry, Mio dear. But perhaps we can find a balance. I am more concerned that if we don't create a space for everyone to gather in the evenings, we might lose more members.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, gathering in the evenings is a goal, but we must consider who is actually providing that space. If we choose a self-catering option, the ""bonding"" time for most is just more labor for the few in charge.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, you're right about the work, but @Shizue, if we're all tired from training at 5 AM or midnight, we'll be too grumpy to bond! We need a place where we can actually sleep and wake up happy!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, we should be cautious. If we set a fixed fee and then have to cover cancellations or hidden costs, the club account will suffer. We need a pricing model that is transparent and stable.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, I totally agree! If the costs are hidden or shift around, some people might end up paying way more than others without even knowing it. We need a system where everyone knows exactly where their money is going!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is so important to be transparent, as you say. But let us not forget the heart of the matter; if the atmosphere is cold, the cost doesn't matter. We must ensure the layout encourages us to talk and laugh together.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, a warm atmosphere is a result of a sustainable system, not a substitute for one. If the organizers are exhausted by nine-page applications and hours of cooking, they cannot contribute to that warmth. We must prioritize operational efficiency.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, you're talking like a robot again! But @Shizue, if we're all exhausted and grumpy, the atmosphere will be cold no matter where we go! We need a place that lets us sleep and have adventures without being tired!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, efficiency is a good goal, but it must be paired with financial predictability. If we prioritize a ""simple"" process that leads to unexpected costs, we are just delaying the problem. We cannot afford any more gaps in the budget.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm starting to think that the ""simple"" way might actually be the most stressful! If we just pay one flat fee but the costs shift, it's not really simple for the people paying. Let's find a way to be fair and happy!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree, Mio. Fairness is not just about the money, but about how we treat one another. If we can find a place that is easy to manage and brings us together, everyone will feel the warmth.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"We must be realistic. ""Warmth"" and ""happiness"" are secondary to the fact that the organizers' time is a finite resource. We cannot choose a destination that requires an excessive administrative or physical burden on a few individuals.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I'm not a robot, I'm just a girl who wants to sleep! If we pick a place that's too hard to manage or has a yucky schedule, we'll all be too sleepy to have any fun! Let's pick the most relaxing one!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree that we should avoid unnecessary stress. However, we must be honest about the financial risks. I will not support any option that leaves the budget open to unpredictable gaps or hidden costs. Let's be precise.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
