63,3,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
64,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Wait, Option C sounds like a dream, but it's so far away! @Mio, remember how transport costs jumped so much in the receipts? Plus, a whole building means those scary non-refundable deposits Misaki mentioned! That's too risky!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is a lovely idea to have our own building, but I worry about the distance. If it is too far, some of our dear members might feel it is too much of a burden to attend. We must be mindful of everyone.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C is the most logical choice for the organizers. By having meals arranged through the owner, we eliminate the cooking duty that drained our members last year. It removes the physical burden of self-catering entirely.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Rin,,"But @Ryuji, if we go to Option A, we'll be training at midnight or 5 AM! That's a total sleep disaster! I don't want us to be grumpy zombies. Option C sounds like a real adventure!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option C is too dangerous. A whole-building let with non-refundable deposits and high transport costs is a recipe for a budget deficit. We cannot risk the club account again. I cannot support it.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, I know you want to avoid the cooking, but @Misaki is right! If someone cancels at the last minute, who pays for their share of the building? It's not fair to leave that to the rest of us!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is a difficult balance, isn't it? While I would love for us to have a cozy place to bond in the evenings, we must ensure that no one feels a financial burden. Perhaps there is a way to be together without such risk.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, the financial risk is a concern, but the human cost of Option B is higher. The municipal system's rigid paperwork and lottery are an administrative nightmare. We cannot ignore the burden placed on those who organize the camp.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, paperwork is boring, but being a zombie is worse! Option B has dorms, which sounds like a big sleepover! As long as we don't have to wake up at 5 AM, I'm okay with it!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, administrative effort is a burden, but a financial deficit is a permanent failure. Option B's public beds are affordable and the costs are predictable. It is a far more stable choice than risking the club's funds on a private lodge.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, you're making a lot of sense! If Option B is affordable and stable, it's way better than worrying about who pays for a cancellation in Option C. I want everyone to feel happy and not stressed about money!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I agree, Mio. If we choose Option B, the shared dormitories could be a wonderful way for the different year-groups to mingle and get to know one another, just as the seniors suggested. It feels like a gentle compromise.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, a ""gentle compromise"" for the group is often a heavy burden for the organizers. The lottery and the nine-page application for Option B are not mere details; they are a significant drain on time. We must prioritize a sustainable workload.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, you're still acting like a robot! Paperwork is just writing things down, but sleep is for our brains! Option A is a no-go because of the crazy hours, and B sounds like a fun sleepover! I vote B!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, your time is valuable, but the club's financial health is non-negotiable. Option B provides the predictability we need to ensure no one is left paying for another's mistake. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm with Rin and Misaki! Option B sounds like a fun sleepover and it's way safer for our wallets. I don't want anyone feeling grumpy about money or cancellations! I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we have found a path that satisfies many of our needs. Option B allows us to stay together in dormitories, which is the best way to encourage our members to bond. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I cannot support Option B. The administrative burden of the lottery and the rigid paperwork is an unacceptable cost to the organizers. Option C is the only choice that ensures a sustainable workload by removing the cooking duty. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, you're so stubborn! But we can't all be zombies just to save you from some paperwork! Option B is the most fair and the most fun! I vote for Option B!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"The consensus is clear. While I understand Ryuji's concerns about the paperwork, the financial risk of Option C is simply too high to ignore. Option B is the only responsible choice for the club's budget. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
